---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import KeyFacts from "../components/KeyFacts.astro";
import Table from "../components/Table.astro";
import UnknownsBox from "../components/UnknownsBox.astro";
import LeadMagnetBand from "../components/LeadMagnetBand.astro";
import ChecklistForm from "../components/ChecklistForm.astro";
import FAQ from "../components/FAQ.astro";
import { getImage } from "astro:assets";
import { verifiedOn } from "../data/pages";
import hero from "../assets/images/lisbon-parque-das-nacoes.webp";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";

const lastVerified = verifiedOn("/hqa-vs-startup-visa-tech-visa");

const description =
  "HQA vs Startup Visa Portugal in 2026: how investment packages, the StartUP Visa and the Tech Visa differ in cost, legal basis, family rules and who they suit.";

const headline = "HQA vs StartUP Visa Portugal: And the Tech Visa";
const pageUrl = "https://portugalhqacitizenship.com/hqa-vs-startup-visa-tech-visa";
const heroAlt = "Parque das Nações waterfront in Lisbon";

const ogImage = await getImage({
  src: hero,
  width: 1200,
  height: 630,
  fit: "cover",
  format: "jpg",
  quality: 82,
  layout: "none",
});

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: "What is the difference between the HQA visa and the StartUP Visa?",
    answer:
      "The HQA route uses article 90 (highly qualified activity). The StartUP Visa uses article 89 and needs acceptance by an IAPMEI-certified incubator. The family rules differ.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is the StartUP Visa cheaper?",
    answer: "There is no investment minimum, but you build and fund your own startup, and incubators may charge fees.",
  },
  {
    question: "What is the Tech Visa?",
    answer: "A route for skilled workers hired by a company certified for the Tech Visa by IAPMEI. It does not need an investment.",
  },
  {
    question: "Which route gets citizenship fastest?",
    answer: "None. All three need 10 years of legal residence for most nationals.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I switch from the StartUP Visa to an HQA permit later?",
    answer:
      "Possibly, if you later meet the highly qualified activity conditions. Ask a Portuguese lawyer, because a change of permit type has its own requirements.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HQA vs Startup Visa Portugal - And the Tech Visa"
  metaTitle="HQA vs Startup Visa Portugal - And the Tech Visa | Portugal HQA Citizenship"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/hqa-vs-startup-visa-tech-visa"
  dateModified={lastVerified}
  ogImage={ogImage.src}
  ogImageAlt={heroAlt}
  ogImageWidth={Number(ogImage.attributes.width ?? 1200)}
  ogImageHeight={Number(ogImage.attributes.height ?? 630)}
  schema={[
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      name: headline,
      description:
        "HQA vs Startup Visa Portugal is a common comparison because the routes look alike: both involve a young company and an incubator. The difference is in the legal basis. HQA packages aim for a residence permit for highly qualified activity under article 90. The StartUP Visa uses article 89, which has different family rules. The Tech Visa is a third route, for people hired by a certified company.",
      url: pageUrl,
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline,
      dateModified: lastVerified,
    },
  ]}
>
  <PageHero
  title={headline}
  photo={hero}
  photoAlt={heroAlt}
  verified={lastVerified}
  path="/hqa-vs-startup-visa-tech-visa"
  maxWidth={960}
  priority
>
  <Breadcrumbs slot="crumbs"
    items={[
        { name: "Home", href: "/" },
        { name: "HQA vs Startup Visa and Tech Visa", href: "/hqa-vs-startup-visa-tech-visa" },
      ]}
  />
  <p class="lead" slot="lead">
      HQA vs Startup Visa Portugal is a common comparison because the routes look alike: both involve a young company and an incubator. The difference is in the legal basis. HQA packages aim for a residence permit for highly qualified activity under article 90. The StartUP Visa uses article 89, which has different family rules. The Tech Visa is a third route, for people hired by a certified company.
    </p>
  <p class="small disclaimer" slot="disclaimer">This page is general information, not legal advice.</p>
</PageHero>

  <Section tone="cream" as="div">
<div class="wide">
    <KeyFacts
      items={[
        {
          lead: "Different articles.",
          text: "HQA uses article 90, the StartUP Visa uses article 89, the Tech Visa uses article 90 through a certified company.",
        },
        {
          lead: "Family rules differ.",
          text: "Article 90 families are exempt from the 2-year wait. Article 89 families are not in that list, so the wait applies unless one of the exceptions does.",
        },
        {
          lead: "Different costs.",
          text: "HQA packages cost about €175,000, reported by providers, October 2026. No government body sets or checks that price. The StartUP Visa has no investment minimum.",
        },
        {
          lead: "All lead to the same citizenship rule.",
          text: "10 years of legal residence for most nationals.",
        },
      ]}
    />
</div>
</Section>

  <Section tone="paper">
    <div class="measure">
      <p>Article 90 families and the 2-year wait are explained on the <a href="/hqa-visa-family">family page</a>. The package price is explained on the <a href="/hqa-visa-cost">cost page</a>. The shared citizenship rule is explained in the <a href="/guides/hqa-visa-citizenship-10-year-rule">citizenship guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream">
<div class="measure">
<h2>The three routes side by side</h2>
      </div>
<div class="wide">
<Table>
        <table>
          <colgroup>
            <col class="label-col" />
            <col />
            <col />
            <col />
          </colgroup>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th></th>
              <th>HQA investment package</th>
              <th>StartUP Visa</th>
              <th>Tech Visa</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Legal basis</th>
              <td>Articles 61 and 90</td>
              <td>Article 89</td>
              <td>Article 90, Portaria 328/2018</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Who it is for</th>
              <td>Investors taking a highly qualified role in a funded project</td>
              <td>Founders with their own startup idea</td>
              <td>Skilled workers hired by a certified company</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Who approves the company</th>
              <td>Provider and its partners</td>
              <td>An incubator certified by IAPMEI</td>
              <td>IAPMEI certifies the employer</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Investment</th>
              <td>About €175,000 (reported by providers, October 2026)</td>
              <td>No minimum; you need funds to support yourself</td>
              <td>None</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Family 2-year wait</th>
              <td>Exempt</td>
              <td>Not exempt</td>
              <td>Exempt</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Citizenship</th>
              <td>10 years (7 for EU nationals and nationals of countries where Portuguese is an official language)</td>
              <td>10 years (7 for EU nationals and nationals of countries where Portuguese is an official language)</td>
              <td>10 years (7 for EU nationals and nationals of countries where Portuguese is an official language)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </Table>
    </div>
</Section>

  <div class="reading">
    <Section tone="paper">
<div class="measure">
      <h2>Which one fits you</h2>
      <h3>HQA investment package</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want a ready-made structure and are willing to pay for it</li>
        <li>You can meet the absence limits on a temporary permit</li>
        <li>You want family members exempt from the 2-year wait</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>StartUP Visa</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You have your own business idea and want to build it</li>
        <li>You can get accepted by a certified incubator</li>
        <li>You accept the 2-year wait for family members</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Tech Visa</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You have a job offer from a Portuguese company certified for the Tech Visa</li>
        <li>You want residence without investing</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="unknowns">
        <UnknownsBox level={3}>
          <p>Some providers describe their packages in ways that sound like the StartUP Visa. Ask in writing which article your application will use. It changes the family rules.</p>
        </UnknownsBox>
      </div>
      <p class="action-line"><Button href="/guides/what-is-hqa-visa" variant="text">What is the HQA visa?</Button></p>
    </div>
</Section>
  </div>

  <LeadMagnetBand
    heading="Compare before you commit"
    paragraph="Our free HQA due diligence checklist helps you compare any package with the StartUP Visa and Tech Visa."
  >
    <ChecklistForm idPrefix="startup-checklist" />
  </LeadMagnetBand>

  <div class="reading end">
    <Section tone="paper">
<div class="measure"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <FAQ items={faqItems} />
    
</div>
</Section>

    <Section tone="cream">
<div class="measure">
      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>This page gives general information, not legal advice. Speak to a qualified Portuguese lawyer before you choose a route.</p>
    </div>
</Section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
